       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and there's no added analgesic benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum for acute or inflammatory use)\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (typical for pain or fever)\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided as 400 mg 4 times daily\n\nIf you do want the 1600 mg dose as written, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, tell me which dose to use and I'll enter it now."
